CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17 --stdlib libc++ -D_LIBCPP_ABI_ALTERNATE_STRING_LAYOUT
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ compare: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
libc++'s alternate string layout, the one Apple uses on arm64: the size of
a short string is a 7-bit bit field after the characters.  It stayed
symbolic after the characters were written, and the comparison's memcmp
did not terminate (four cbmc-cpp timeouts on macOS 14).  See
regression/cbmc/union_bit_field_after_other_byte_updates.
